      "textColor": "#000000",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "textAutoWidth": false,
      "text": "**How collaboration works**\n\nThe host opens a document with their Git credentials and clicks Invite collaborators.\nThey share a link. Guests join with just a name — no account, no token, nothing to install.\nEveryone edits the same board live: cursors, selections, and changes appear in real time.\nSharing is scoped — invite people to a single board, a chapter, or the whole document.\nThe host owns saving to Git; guests edit freely, and the host commits the result.\nInvite links have a lifetime you choose (1–30 days) and can be revoked anytime."
    },
